# Red probe — the base commit's engine (2e732f0e00fa771d04569483ffe80bc2ca3fa974), 2026-10-20
#
# The engine was extracted read-only (`git archive HEAD tools/issues | tar -x -C /tmp/red231`) so the
# worktree's fix could not be involved, and driven from the repository root so `issues_resolve` sees a git
# tree. The stub `gh` (this change's transient injection) is first on PATH; delays are irrelevant here
# because the base commit has no retry.

## 1. The identity read fails the way a socket does — policy.sh answers a refusal it never established

$ GH_STUB_TRANSIENT_FAIL="api user" GH_STUB_TRANSIENT_TIMES=99 ... bash /tmp/red231/tools/issues/policy.sh preflight --json
{
  "login": "",
  "decision": "refuse",
  "reason": "author-not-allowlisted",
  "detail": "(no authenticated login)"
}
exit=3

## 2. One read fails transiently twice, a third attempt would answer — the outage becomes an empty set

$ GH_STUB_TRANSIENT_FAIL="issue list" GH_STUB_TRANSIENT_TIMES=2 ... bash /tmp/red231/tools/issues/list.sh --json --limit 1
exit=0
attempts made by HEAD: 1
Post "https://api.github.com/graphql": dial tcp 20.250.119.72:443: i/o timeout

## The same two probes against the fixed engine

1. `policy.sh preflight --json` -> {"login":"","decision":"unknown","reason":"tracker-unreachable",
   "detail":"(the tracker API did not answer — no identity could be read)"}, exit 75
   (case `policy#preflightReportsAnUnreachableTracker`)
2. `lib#retriesATransientFailure` — the third attempt's answer arrives, the stub counted two failures.

## 3. The change's own cases, run against the base commit's engine (2026-10-20)

$ bash /tmp/red231/redcases.sh     # only ISSUES_ENGINE points at the base commit's extracted tree
RED-OK   case_lib_exitCodeConstants failed on the base commit: the exit-code contract: expected '0 2 3 4 75', got ''
RED-OK   case_lib_retriesATransientFailure failed on the base commit: the retried call returns the answer, not the outage: expected 'Framstag', got ''
RED-OK   case_lib_reportsAnUnreachableTrackerAfterTheLastRetry failed on the base commit: 'status:75' not found in: status:1
RED-MISS case_lib_doesNotRetryAnAuthoritativeFailure passed on the base commit
RED-OK   case_policy_preflightReportsAnUnreachableTracker failed on the base commit: expected '75', got '3'

Four of the five are red on the base commit. The fifth is the guard the fix must not break — the base commit
never retries anything, so "an authoritative refusal is not retried" holds there vacuously; it goes red if
the seam ever retries a refusal.
